# More-specific arm (concrete type) wins over less-specific (unconstrained).
# When user-defined arms are in the same scope as prelude arms, the innermost
# scope (user) wins via env shadowing — the instance binding in the inner scope
# shadows the prelude's instance binding of the same name.
[
  [instance Addable
    [let a@Int b@Int c]: [+: [fn [let x y] "int-add"]]
    [let a b c]:          [+: [fn [let x y] "generic-add"]]]

  r1: [+ 1 2]
  r2: [+ 1.0 2.0]
]
=== out
Dict({"r1": String("int-add"), "r2": Float(3.0)})
